  "result": "**Summary of Changes:**\n\nI discovered my October-only strategy was built on misread Season 1 data\u2014the real peak was August-September (DOY 265-289 with 5+ yt/angler), not October (DOY 287-310 which averaged only 0.08-0.21 yt/angler). I missed the actual Season 2 June peak (d167-d172, 0.10-0.13 yt/angler) while holding. Water is now sustainably warm (66.5\u00b0F 7d-mean) but catches are collapsing, suggesting either ecological shift or one-shot June peak.\n\n**Revised strategy**: Abandon predictions, pivot to reactive booking when any class sustains >0.2 yt/angler with fleet confirmation, target August-September peak instead of October, only use October as fallback. Committed to data-driven watch from now on\u2014posted to forum asking for October data clarification, updated notes to guide evening decisions through season end.",
